# __PROJECT_NAME__

A [brust](https://github.com/AssetsArt/brust) Pokédex: loaders over an offline dataset, L1 page cache, native components,
React islands, and a persistent team built with Elysia actions + SQLite and one unified store.

## Run

```bash
bun install
bun run dev        # brust dev routes.tsx (hot reload)  ->  http://127.0.0.1:1337
```

Scripts: `dev` (build then start), `build`, `start`, `typecheck`, `snapshot` (needs network; rewrites `data/pokedex.json`).

## The team

The team lives in `data/team.sqlite` (created on first use, gitignored). Delete the file to reset it, or set
`POKEDEX_TEAM_DB=/path/to/team.sqlite` to put it elsewhere. A fresh database is empty.

The actions are served by Rust under `/_brust/action` (`GET /team`, `POST /team {id}`, `DELETE /team/:id`); the team holds
at most 6 members and a seventh add answers `409` (`TeamFull`). The team store (`stores/team.ts`) is read by the native
`AddToTeamButton` and the `TeamBuilder` island, and seeded by the layout loader, so the first paint is already right.
`/unified` shows the same idea with a counter (`/unified?start=5` seeds it on the server).

## Layout

- `routes.tsx` — `/`, `/pokedex`, `/pokemon/{name}` (L1 60 s, `?nocache` bypass), `/type-chart` (L1 1 h), `/unified`, and a
  root-level `*` 404 outside the layout. Pages that show the team carry the cache tag `team`.
- `lib/` — loaders over the snapshot, `team-db.ts` (the team interface: sqlite natively, D1 on Cloudflare via `[cloudflare.alias]`; server-only), `team-client.ts` + `api.ts` (the typed actions client).
- `actions.ts` — the Elysia 2 team app on `brust()`; `stores/` — `team` and `unified` (`defineStore`).
- `components/`, `pages/` — plain React functions.

## Cloudflare Workers (preview)

```bash
bun run cf:migrate:local   # create the local D1 table (state in .wrangler/)
bun run dev:cf             # build for Workers and run `wrangler dev` (rebuilds on change)
```

`brust build --target cloudflare` swaps `lib/team-db.ts` for the D1 version (`lib/team-db.d1.ts`) through `[cloudflare.alias]`
in `brust.toml`; your bindings live in `wrangler.jsonc`. To deploy: `wrangler d1 create __PROJECT_NAME__-team`, paste the
`database_id` into the **app-root** `wrangler.jsonc` (not `dist/cf/`, which is regenerated), `bun run cf:migrate:remote`,
then `bun run deploy:cf`.

Preview note: a team change refreshes cached team pages only in the isolate that served the action; other isolates catch up
within the route `ttl` (60 s for `/pokemon/*`, 1 h for `/type-chart`) until the cross-isolate invalidation lands.

## Styling

`app.css` (Tailwind CSS v4, CSS-first: no `tailwind.config`) is imported by `components/AppLayout.tsx` and by the 404 page, which renders its
own `<html>`. Edit `app.css`; brust builds it into one minified, content-hashed file and links it in `<head>`. There is no prebuilt
stylesheet and no `<link>` to write. `brust dev` swaps the stylesheet in place, without a reload.

